.TH tutablepng 1 0.1 tclutils "Tcl Utility Command"
.SH NAME
tutablepng \- thin CLI wrapper for tclutils::tutablepng
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tutablepng <out.png> ?-d DELIM? ?-header 0|1? ?-align SPEC? ?file?
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The tutablepng command renders delimited rows (from a file or standard input)
as a styled PNG table, via the Tcl package tclutils::tutablepng and the pure-Tcl
drawing layer tclutils::tupngdraw. The primary interface is the Tcl library;
see tutablepng(n) for procedures, options and semantics.
.PP
.nf
tclsh bin/tutablepng.tcl out.png -d , -header 1 -align "l r r" data.csv
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tupngdraw(n), tupng(n)
